This paper introduces a method for embedding a group $G$ into a wreath product $H \wr S_n$ by utilizing the Cartesian decomposition of $G$. We demonstrate that this approach yields a more efficient embedding than the standard one for the symmetric group $S_n$ when $n$ is sufficiently large. Furthermore, we apply this technique to construct an embedding of the symmetric group $S_n$ into the wreath product $S_m \wr S_n$ for any $m \geq 2$. Finally, we establish that the wreath product $S_m \wr S_n$ is a subgroup of the wreath product $S_{m^2} \wr S_n$.
