We present a method to explicitly determine Serre weights for the group $GL_2$ over a totally real field $F$, utilizing the explicit construction of the Galois representation associated with a Hilbert modular form. This approach relies on the explicit Kummer theory of the field $F(\mu_p)$, where $\mu_p$ denotes the group of $p$-th roots of unity. Furthermore, we demonstrate that the weights identified through this method are the sole weights compatible with the local conditions at $p$ for the Galois representation linked to a Hilbert modular form. Finally, we apply this technique to compute the weights for the case where $F = \mathbb{Q}$.
